Z||000000||80's BOY||12-24-2000||05:41 PM||||one day i was selling some junk iron to the local small-town junk collector (an elderly spanish man). so i back up my truck, and what do i see but an 84 4cyl gold fiero with a sunroof sitting in the weeds. i ask him "will you sell the car?" he says no..no..mucho metal aqui!" as he taps on the hood. he thought it was metal!! so i TRIED to eplain to him F I B E R G L A S S but he didn't understand the concept. so i say "sellee for fifty dollars!!" and hold out some money. he says " no sellee the car...mucho money aqui!" frustrated, i went about my business and went back home. and I'll BE DAMNED if i didn't see that car at a stop light last week, with some kid driving it!! i asked the kid how he got the car, and he said he traded a load of old car batteries for it to a mexican across town. CAR BATTERIES????? all the kid did was buy a new injector for the tbi and a new battery, cranked it up and drove it away. man, what a rip. anyway, i see that thing all the time now. stupid small town B.S.||||reg||8
