Z||000003||BAM-BAM||12-24-2000||09:55 PM||||  The fiberglass explanation was due to the fact the the hispanic gentleman was rapping on the hood stating "Much Metal Here", when infact the hood, deck lid and top are fiberglass. The vetical panels and the facias are plastic. However, maybe the old guy knew that everything underneeth was metal. Still, a bunch of old batteries? Geez, I guess what they say is true; "One mans junk is another mans treasure". Hey, I think I just happened on a new country song! "One mans junk is another mans treasure, one mans pleasure is another mans pain". Well, gotta go, need to figure out the rest of those lyrics.<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
